<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-QA-105>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-QA-105" ;
  triage:title "Dead HERDR_WAKE_TEXT constant violates AX.2 acceptance criterion 1" ;
  triage:description "The develop freshness merge kept the HERDR_WAKE_TEXT constant that develop still uses (lib.rs:643, :1054 on develop 550627d71) while Phase AX removed every use of it, leaving an unused pub const at 3afa39160. AX.2 acceptance criterion 1 requires `grep -rn HERDR_WAKE_TEXT crates docs/adr docs/atm-herdr docs/requirements.md docs/architecture.md boundaries` to return nothing; docs/plans/phase-ax/*.md mentions are the plan itself and are excluded by that grep only for docs/plans, so the const line is the sole violation. Remediation: delete the constant (and any test that referenced only it) on stack #1235; re-run the literal grep and quote it. No earlier QA round caught it because the const arrived from develop after AX.2 closed." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
